      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Shared procedure for 1–3 (SI): LnCl3·6H2O (1 equiv.; Ln = Tb, Dy, Er) was added to a stirring solution of LH3 (1 equiv.) in 10 mL methanol. After about 30 min, triethylamine (3 equiv.) was added, giving a yellow clear solution. Dibenzoylmethane (1 equiv.) was then added, turning the mixture turbid, and stirring was continued for 6 h. The solution was evaporated to dryness in vacuo, redissolved in methanol/chloroform (1:1), and filtered. Slow evaporation of the filtrate afforded red block crystals. For 1: LH3 (0.036 g, 0.140 mmol), TbCl3·6H2O (0.052 g, 0.140 mmol), dbm (0.031 g, 0.140 mmol), NEt3 (0.078 mL, 4 mmol as reported).",
