      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility (2–300 K, 1000 Oe) shows chi_M T = 91.28 cm3 K mol-1 at 300 K (calc. 82.74 for seven uncoupled Tb3+), remaining nearly constant to 110 K then dropping to 53.16 cm3 K mol-1 at 2 K, consistent with overall antiferromagnetic interactions plus Stark depopulation. Curie–Weiss fit (2–300 K): C = 9.62, theta = -2.88. Magnetization at 2 K rises rapidly then more slowly to 43.86 μB at 7 T without saturation.",
