      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc chi_M T at 300 K agrees with seven isolated Dy3+ (99.19 cm3 K mol-1). On cooling, chi_M T rises to 105.44 cm3 K mol-1 at 120 K, falls to 100.29 cm3 K mol-1 at 24 K, then increases sharply to 139.80 cm3 K mol-1 at 2 K, indicating ferromagnetic interactions at low T. Curie–Weiss (300–2 K): C = 101.52, theta = 0.98. M(H) at 2 K reaches 43.06 μB at 7 T without saturation. Zero-dc-field ac data show frequency-dependent chi'' without a maximum above 2 K; under 5000 Oe, frequency-dependent peaks appear. Estimated U_eff = 4.84 K and tau_0 = 2.56e-5 s.",
